---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Alternative Matting Laplacian - François Pitié" currentSection="research">
  <div class="mb-8 pb-3 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#0569B9] dark:text-[#82B4DC] mb-1">
      <a href="/research" class="hover:underline">&larr; Back to Research & Projects</a>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
      The Alternative Matting Laplacian
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1">
      Direct parameter diffusion and closed-form formulation for natural image matting.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Theory & Formulation Section -->
  <section class="space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-8">
    <p>
      In natural image matting, an observed linear RGB colour $C_i$ at pixel $i$ is modelled as a convex combination of an unknown foreground colour $F_i$ and background colour $B_i$:
    </p>
    <div class="p-3 rounded bg-slate-200/60 dark:bg-slate-800/60 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-center text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
      C_i = &alpha;_i F_i + (1 - &alpha;_i) B_i
    </div>
    <p>
      Under the widely adopted local color-line assumption pioneered by Levin et al., the local transparency values are approximated as an affine transformation of the color components:
    </p>
    <div class="p-3 rounded bg-slate-200/60 dark:bg-slate-800/60 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-center text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
      &alpha;_i = a_i^T C_i + b_i
    </div>
    <p>
      While classical approaches eliminate the local vector $a_i$ and offset $b_i$ to solve implicitly for $\alpha$ via the Levin Matting Laplacian, our work takes the exact opposite approach: <strong>we explicitly solve for the model parameters $a$ and $b$</strong>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Visual Grid of Results -->
  <section class="mb-10 space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white pb-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      Visualizing Model Parameters and Alpha Mattes
    </h2>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-2">
        <img src="/images/troll.jpg" alt="Original Troll Image" class="w-full h-auto rounded" />
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1 text-center font-medium">Input Test Image (alphamatting.com)</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-2">
        <img src="/images/troll_colourfilter.jpg" alt="Colour Filter Visualization" class="w-full h-auto rounded" />
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1 text-center font-medium">Revealing &alpha; through Local Colour Filter</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-2">
        <img src="/images/troll_a_ours.jpg" alt="Diffused Model Parameter a" class="w-full h-auto rounded" />
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1 text-center font-medium">Our Parameter Map (a) with Smoothness Priors</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-2">
        <img src="/images/troll_alpha_ours.jpg" alt="Extracted Alpha Matte" class="w-full h-auto rounded" />
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1 text-center font-medium">Extracted Alpha Matte (&alpha;)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Advantages & Key Insight -->
  <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white pb-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      Key Advantages
    </h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base">
      <li>
        <strong>Computational Simplicity:</strong> The problem naturally simplifies into anisotropic diffusion of $a$ and $b$, leading to simpler and faster sparse linear systems.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Meaningful Priors:</strong> Because the colour filter vectors are exposed explicitly, spatial smoothness and boundary-preserving regularization can be imposed directly on the parameters.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Foundation for Neural Multigrid Solvers:</strong> Forms the algebraic foundation for contemporary deep learning matting systems including fastAML and dual-stream neural V-cycle architectures.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Code & Paper Links -->
  <section class="mb-10 p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-200/60 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-700/80">
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
      <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[#0569B9] dark:text-[#82B4DC]" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.484 2 12.017c0 4.425 2.865 8.18 6.839 9.504.5.092.682-.217.682-.483 0-.237-.008-.868-.013-1.703-2.782.605-3.369-1.343-3.369-1.343-.454-1.158-1.11-1.466-1.11-1.466-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.53 1.032 1.53 1.032.892 1.53 2.341 1.088 2.91.832.092-.647.35-1.088.636-1.338-2.22-.253-4.555-1.113-4.555-4.951 0-1.093.39-1.988 1.029-2.688-.103-.253-.446-1.272.098-2.65 0 0 .84-.27 2.75 1.026A9.564 9.564 0 0112 6.844c.85.004 1.705.115 2.504.337 1.909-1.296 2.747-1.027 2.747-1.027.546 1.379.202 2.398.1 2.651.64.7 1.028 1.595 1.028 2.688 0 3.848-2.339 4.695-4.566 4.943.359.309.678.92.678 1.855 0 1.338-.012 2.419-.012 2.747 0 .268.18.58.688.482A10.019 10.019 0 0022 12.017C22 6.484 17.522 2 12 2z"/>
      </svg>
      Code & Preprint
    </h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-[#0569B9] dark:text-[#82B4DC]">
      <a href="https://github.com/frcs/alternative-matting-laplacian" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 hover:underline">
        GitHub Repository &rarr;
      </a>
      <span>&bull;</span>
      <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.04785" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 hover:underline">
        arXiv:1605.04785 &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Citation -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white pb-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 mb-3">
      Reference Publication
    </h2>
    <div class="border-l-2 border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pl-3.5 py-0.5 hover:border-[#0569B9] transition-colors">
      <div class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
        The Alternative Matting Laplacian
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">
        François Pitié
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">
        <em>2016 IEEE International Conference on Image Processing (ICIP)</em>, Phoenix, AZ, 2016.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
